      "mergeID": "5eac60804e2d593e896ba02f",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Add the ability to copy or cut a node with its relative offset to the centre of the udon window, rather than its position within the graph.\nThis way you can paste a node in where you currently are in the graph rather than having to find the node which could be nowhere near where you are working in the graph. It would just paste it relative to the current centre of the window. It would still allow complete graphs to be copied, it would just make it much easier to paste them into new graphs or into existing ones when you know it will be placed where you are in the graph.\nWould be handy to have as keyboard shortcuts such as [Ctrl+Alt+C] and [Ctrl+Alt+X]. However, it is fine to only have it as a right click menu item.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Copy and cut nodes with position relative to window centre rather than graph",
